1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:07,090
Seventy-five point two percent sounds impressive, but first identify exactly what was tested.
75.2%很亮眼，但先确认测的是什么。

2
00:00:07,510 --> 00:00:12,770
This averages seven complete teleoperation tasks using the five-finger SharpaWave hand.
这是五指SharpaWave完成七项遥操作任务的平均值。

3
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:16,750
A human still supplies the intended motion throughout these experiments.
这些实验始终由人提供运动意图。

4
00:00:17,170 --> 00:00:23,030
Each task has fifteen trials, so one success changes its score by almost seven percentage points.
每项15次试验，一次成功就改变近7个百分点。

5
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:29,030
These results demonstrate useful control under this protocol, rather than general autonomous manipulation.
这些结果说明该协议下控制有效，不能推出通用自主操作。

6
00:00:29,777 --> 00:00:35,157
Consider a hammer trial that completes five stages, then fails before the final two.
假设一次锤子试验完成五步，最后两步失败。

7
00:00:35,397 --> 00:00:40,057
Its success contribution is zero, because the entire sequence was not completed.
它对成功率的贡献为零，因为流程没有全部完成。

8
00:00:40,557 --> 00:00:45,657
Its task progress contribution is five sevenths, because earlier stages still count.
任务进度贡献是七分之五，已完成步骤仍计分。

9
00:00:45,977 --> 00:00:50,257
Average these quantities across all fifteen trials to obtain the reported metrics.
将这两个量分别对15次试验取平均，就得到表中指标。

10
00:00:50,757 --> 00:00:56,497
Progress rewards partial completion; it does not measure speed, throughput, or precise tracking error.
进度计入部分完成，不代表速度、吞吐量或精确跟踪误差。

11
00:00:56,987 --> 00:01:03,547
The three reorientation tasks require picking up, rotating, and placing an object back down.
三项重定向任务都要求拿起、转向，再放回物体。

12
00:01:03,967 --> 00:01:08,067
The tool tasks add interaction with the environment and further changes of grip.
工具任务还加入环境交互，以及后续的换握。

13
00:01:08,207 --> 00:01:12,207
Hammering, for example, continues through pulling nails and returning the hammer.
例如锤子任务还要拔钉，并把锤子放回。

14
00:01:12,627 --> 00:01:16,847
A convincing middle step therefore cannot stand in for complete task success.
因此，中途某一步很漂亮，不等于整个任务成功。

15
00:01:17,307 --> 00:01:22,307
Also notice the bandage tape: these experimental objects receive added surface friction.
还要注意绷带胶带：实验对物体表面摩擦做了增强。

16
00:01:22,875 --> 00:01:28,455
Figure six follows how many of the original fifteen trials reach each successive stage.
Figure 6记录最初15次试验中，有多少到达后续各阶段。

17
00:01:28,895 --> 00:01:32,595
Read its horizontal axis as task stages, not elapsed time.
横轴是任务阶段，不是经过的时间。

18
00:01:33,035 --> 00:01:38,955
For bulb replacement, all fifteen reach the fourth stage, while thirteen finish the complete sequence.
灯泡任务15次都到达第四步，最后13次完成全流程。

19
00:01:39,615 --> 00:01:44,535
The drop appears during the final return phase, after the bulb has been unscrewed.
下降出现在旋出灯泡之后的最后放回流程中。

20
00:01:44,775 --> 00:01:48,915
That localizes a bottleneck more clearly than a single headline percentage.
这比单独一个总成功率，更能定位薄弱环节。

21
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:55,400
Before ranking methods, inspect which tasks and implementations actually enter the comparison.
排名之前，先看比较实际包含了哪些任务和实现。

22
00:01:56,120 --> 00:02:01,640
SimToolReal is evaluated on three tool tasks, so its average covers a different task set.
SimToolReal只测三项工具任务，其平均值覆盖范围不同。

23
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:07,500
The authors also reimplement DexGen and replace one rollout component with their own controller.
作者还重新实现DexGen，并用自己的控制器替换一处轨迹生成模块。

24
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:11,840
These choices matter when interpreting the size of the reported advantage.
理解性能优势有多大时，这些选择都很重要。

25
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:17,800
The table supports a comparison under this setup, not a universal ranking across robotics.
表格支持的是此设置下的比较，不能变成整个机器人的通用排名。

26
00:02:18,473 --> 00:02:24,773
The second robot hand provides a useful test of the overall pipeline across different morphologies.
第二种机器人手检验了这套流程能否适配不同形态。

27
00:02:25,433 --> 00:02:28,753
LeapHand has four fingers, compared with five on SharpaWave.
LeapHand是四指，而SharpaWave是五指。

28
00:02:29,113 --> 00:02:34,693
The same human references are reused, but retargeting and controller training remain hand specific.
两者复用人类参考动作，但重定向和控制器训练仍分别进行。

29
00:02:35,313 --> 00:02:41,413
LeapHand completes sixty percent of cylinder trials and seventy-three point three percent of cuboid trials.
LeapHand圆柱任务成功率60%，长方体为73.3%。

30
00:02:42,013 --> 00:02:47,253
These are two evaluated tasks, not the complete seven-task benchmark transferred unchanged.
这里只评测了两项任务，并非原封不动迁移整套七任务基准。

31
00:02:48,103 --> 00:02:55,443
The any-to-any experiment asks whether a grasp can transition between targets sampled from recorded reference frames.
Any-to-any检验抓握能否在已记录参考帧采样的目标之间转换。

32
00:02:56,283 --> 00:03:01,323
Success requires object position within two centimeters and orientation within twenty degrees.
成功要求物体位置误差小于2厘米，朝向误差小于20度。

33
00:03:01,963 --> 00:03:06,483
Each active target receives up to twenty seconds before the trial terminates.
当前目标最多尝试20秒，超时就结束试验。

34
00:03:06,983 --> 00:03:13,223
Cylinder trials average forty-one point one consecutive targets; cuboid trials average twelve point one.
圆柱平均连续完成41.1个目标，长方体为12.1个。

35
00:03:13,423 --> 00:03:18,903
That tests new transitions within reference coverage, not arbitrary unseen objects or poses.
它检验参考覆盖范围内的新转换，不代表任意未知物体或姿态。

36
00:03:19,492 --> 00:03:26,872
Table four compares sparse-goal training with dense tracking, then evaluates both controllers in two different ways.
Table 4比较稀疏目标与密集跟踪训练，再用两种方式评估。

37
00:03:27,192 --> 00:03:31,232
In dense evaluation, a new reference arrives every control step.
密集评估在每个控制步更新参考。

38
00:03:31,752 --> 00:03:36,552
In sparse evaluation, the next target arrives only after the current target is reached.
稀疏评估只有达到当前目标，才给出下一个目标。

39
00:03:36,872 --> 00:03:42,592
For the hammer, sparse training reaches one hundred eighty-six point six goals, versus two point seven.
锤子稀疏评估中，稀疏训练完成186.6个目标，对照为2.7个。

40
00:03:42,812 --> 00:03:47,612
Compare matching columns: episode length and completed goals are different quantities.
应在同一列比较：回合长度和完成目标数不是同一量。

41
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:53,900
Action masking occasionally holds selected joint commands at their previous values during training.
动作屏蔽会在训练时，偶尔让部分关节命令保持上一值。

42
00:03:54,340 --> 00:03:58,840
It encourages the controller to cope when the commanded motion is not fully executed.
它鼓励控制器适应指令运动未完全执行的情况。

43
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:05,780
For the screwdriver, removing this mechanism reduces complete success from seventy-three point three percent to zero.
螺丝刀任务去掉该机制，完整成功率从73.3%降到零。

44
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:09,900
Hammer and cuboid performance also decline in the reported ablation.
论文的消融中，锤子和长方体性能也下降。

45
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:16,059
This supports its benefit here, without isolating which physical actuator defect it compensates for.
这支持它在此处有效，但没有单独确定补偿了哪种执行器缺陷。

46
00:04:16,509 --> 00:04:22,869
Figure five separates the full training recipe from versions without the curriculum or without SAPG.
Figure 5对比完整训练方案、去掉课程，以及去掉SAPG。

47
00:04:23,029 --> 00:04:28,149
Follow the curves across environment steps, rather than comparing a single attractive endpoint.
应沿环境步数观察曲线，而非只挑一个漂亮终点。

48
00:04:28,589 --> 00:04:33,609
The full recipe achieves higher reward and more consecutive successes in this hammer experiment.
在这项锤子实验中，完整方案获得更高奖励和更多连续成功。

49
00:04:34,069 --> 00:04:39,209
However, the plot does not show error bands or variation across independent training seeds.
但图中没有误差带，也没有独立训练种子间的波动。

50
00:04:39,409 --> 00:04:43,429
Treat the ordering as evidence from the reported runs, not a universal guarantee.
因此，排序是已报告运行的证据，不是普遍保证。

51
00:04:44,155 --> 00:04:51,055
The autonomous results come from a separate learning stage using demonstrations collected through teleoperation.
自主结果来自另一个学习阶段，数据通过遥操作收集。

52
00:04:51,655 --> 00:04:57,935
Each task receives fifty expert robot demonstrations, followed by fifteen evaluation trials.
每项任务收集50条专家机器人示范，再做15次评测。

53
00:04:58,315 --> 00:05:04,195
A diffusion policy uses third-person and wrist RGB observations with frozen visual encoders.
扩散策略使用第三视角和腕部RGB观测，以及冻结的视觉编码器。

54
00:05:04,595 --> 00:05:08,140
Two observation frames condition a prediction of sixteen actions.
两帧观测用于预测16个动作。

55
00:05:08,155 --> 00:05:15,235
This is task-specific imitation learning, not the original teleoperation controller suddenly operating without a person.
这是针对任务的模仿学习，并非原遥操作控制器直接去掉人。

56
00:05:15,866 --> 00:05:21,506
In the autonomy table, each stage reports survivors relative to the previous stage.
自主结果表中，每一阶段的分母是上一阶段存活数。

57
00:05:21,826 --> 00:05:27,946
For bulb installation, fifteen attempts shrink to thirteen, then twelve, then eight, and finally seven.
灯泡安装从15次，依次剩下13、12、8，最后7次。

58
00:05:28,346 --> 00:05:33,446
Seven out of eight at the last stage therefore does not mean eighty-seven percent overall success.
最后一步的八分之七，并不代表整体成功率87%。

59
00:05:34,006 --> 00:05:38,566
Overall success remains seven out of fifteen, or forty-six point seven percent.
整体仍是十五分之七，即46.7%。

60
00:05:38,986 --> 00:05:44,086
The largest intermediate loss occurs at alignment, giving us a concrete target for improvement.
中间损失最多的是对准阶段，这给出了具体改进方向。

61
00:05:44,836 --> 00:05:50,896
Do not compare the autonomous hammer score directly against the complete teleoperation hammer score.
不能直接拿自主锤子分数，对比完整遥操作锤子分数。

62
00:05:51,516 --> 00:05:57,116
The autonomous version uses larger nails and foam, and omits pulling nails and returning the tool.
自主版使用更大钉子和泡沫，并省去拔钉、放回工具。

63
00:05:57,776 --> 00:06:01,576
Bulb installation omits unscrewing and the final return sequence.
灯泡安装省去了旋出和最后放回流程。

64
00:06:01,936 --> 00:06:04,876
Brushing also becomes a shorter forward-sweeping task.
刷扫也变为较短的向前扫任务。

65
00:06:05,476 --> 00:06:12,256
These experiments establish a demonstration-learning pathway, while leaving harder autonomous sequences for further validation.
这些实验建立了示范学习路径，更难的自主长流程仍待验证。

66
00:06:12,962 --> 00:06:21,282
The failure examples separate external disturbances, jammed contact transitions, and tracking that stalls without dropping the object.
失败案例分为外部扰动、换接触卡住，以及不掉物却停滞。

67
00:06:21,902 --> 00:06:26,212
A hammer impact can push the hand-object state outside familiar training conditions.
锤击可能把手和物体推离熟悉的训练状态。

68
00:06:27,202 --> 00:06:30,382
A finger that fails to lift can obstruct the next grasp.
未成功抬离的手指，可能阻碍下一次换握。

69
00:06:30,882 --> 00:06:35,287
Missing tactile feedback may also leave sliding and pressing difficult to distinguish.
缺少触觉反馈，也可能难以区分滑动和按压。

70
00:06:35,302 --> 00:06:43,519
These are representative mechanisms and author interpretations, not measured failure frequencies or proof that touch alone solves them.
这是代表性机制和作者解释，并非频率统计或触觉单独解决问题的证明。

71
00:06:43,969 --> 00:06:51,609
For each object, the dataset contains one hundred fifty twenty-second trajectories, or fifty minutes of human motion.
每个物体有150条、每条20秒的轨迹，合计50分钟人类动作。

72
00:06:52,049 --> 00:06:58,989
Each controller then requires its own training, reported at roughly one day on four RTX fifty-ninety GPUs.
每个控制器还要分别训练，论文报告约需4张RTX 5090训练一天。

73
00:06:59,489 --> 00:07:04,849
Deployment retains optical markers, object tracking, calibration, and the human operator.
部署仍保留光学标记、物体跟踪、标定和操作者。

74
00:07:05,349 --> 00:07:09,954
These requirements are part of the system, rather than incidental laboratory decoration.
这些要求属于系统本身，不是无关的实验室布置。

75
00:07:09,969 --> 00:07:14,589
A new object therefore adds both data collection and policy-training work.
因此，新物体仍需要增加采集数据和训练策略的工作。

76
00:07:15,048 --> 00:07:22,028
Start reproduction with one object and the original stage definitions, then log every trial through completion or failure.
复现先选一个物体，沿用原阶段定义，逐次记录成功或失败。

77
00:07:22,268 --> 00:07:27,408
Match friction, sensing, target tolerances, and control timing before changing the method.
修改方法之前，先对齐摩擦、感知、目标容差和控制节拍。

78
00:07:27,648 --> 00:07:32,888
Clarify the appendix discrepancy between thirty-hertz capture and sixty-hertz reference timing.
附录30赫兹采集与60赫兹参考节拍的差异，需要先澄清。

79
00:07:33,088 --> 00:07:38,373
Also request the unspecified tolerance-curriculum schedule before claiming an exact replication.
宣称精确复现前，还应确认未明确列出的容差课程日程。

80
00:07:38,388 --> 00:07:44,988
The strongest takeaway is a practical bridge from human targets to contact-rich control, with clearly bounded evidence.
最有力的结论，是把人类目标接到复杂接触控制上的实用路径。
